1
00:00:03,401 --> 00:00:07,679
Re-measure before cutting: the Ortiz back wall is 119", not 121".

2
00:00:07,679 --> 00:00:13,135
Record the revision in the job notes first.

3
00:00:13,135 --> 00:00:26,054
On the Room tab, type the new width.

4
00:00:26,054 --> 00:00:30,732
The app flags it straight away: the 3-5/16" filler F1 now runs past the wall.

5
00:00:30,732 --> 00:00:38,965
The filler was cut to the old gap, so remove it: Cabinets tab, the bin on F1.

6
00:00:38,965 --> 00:00:46,741
Back in the room, the run is now 1-5/16" short of the 119" wall, and the app measures it.

7
00:00:46,741 --> 00:00:52,135
Fill gap makes a new filler of exactly that width.

8
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:56,494
The warning is gone: the run meets the 119" wall again. Nothing else had to change.

9
00:00:56,494 --> 00:01:02,049
Elevation of the back wall, with the narrower filler at the right end.

10
00:01:02,049 --> 00:01:12,332
The cut list picks up the new filler size...

11
00:01:12,332 --> 00:01:18,127
...and nesting re-runs, so the labels and sheet maps match the revised job.

12
00:01:18,127 --> 00:01:22,329
A site change caught before cutting: one number in the room, one new filler, done.
